      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Saint Rose of Lima, the patron saint of the Americas, and the original plantation bearing that name survived until 1904.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://scphistory.org/st-rose-town-history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The LaBranche Plantation Dependency House, a surviving 18th‑century building, sits in St. Rose and is listed on the National Historic Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://scphistory.org/st-rose-town-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The main house of LaBranche Plantation was built by the Zweig family in 1792 and was a center for sugar‑cane cultivation and processing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://scphistory.org/st-rose-town-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "St. Rose is the hometown of NFL star Justin Jefferson, the Minnesota Vikings wide receiver who was drafted in 2018.",
